    "fabric": {
      "capacityMbps": 176000,
      "kind": "switching fabric",
      "note": "Vendor switching capacity of 176 Gbps with a 130.95 Mpps maximum forwarding rate. 48 gigabit ports plus four ten-gigabit ports is 48 x 2 + 4 x 20 = 176 Gbps full duplex, and 130.95 Mpps is 48 x 1.488 plus 4 x 14.88, so the vendor forwarding rate follows the port count exactly."
    },
    "notes": "Ports, per the D-Link DGS-1520 Series A1 datasheet: 48 x 10/100/1000Base-T, 2 x 10GBase-T, 2 x 10G SFP+. No PoE - the PoE rows are N/A for this model. Maximum consumption 51.2 W, standby 25.5 W at 100 V / 26.8 W at 240 V, heat 174.6 BTU/hr, 56.8 dB(A), MTBF 364,888 hours, 441 x 207.4 x 44 mm, 2.78 kg. Takes the DPS-520 redundant supply, for non-PoE models only. Ports are named by media because the datasheet publishes the census, not a front-panel index. Vendor software, same document: physical stacking of up to 8 units over 10GBase-T and/or SFP+ at up to 80 Gbps in ring or chain, virtual stacking (Single IP Management) of up to 32 units, 16,384 MAC entries (512 static), jumbo frames to 12,288 bytes, 32 LACP groups of 8 ports, 802.1D/802.1w/802.1s STP with BPDU filtering, root guard and loop guard, ERPS v1/v2, RSPAN, 4K VLAN groups (VID 1-4094) including selective Q-in-Q and VLAN translation, IGMP v1/v2/v3 snooping, MLD v1/v2 snooping, and L3 routing - static routes, RIP/RIPng, OSPF, VRRP v2/v3, PIM-SM/DM/SSM, 1024 hardware routing entries and 4096 L3 forwarding entries shared by IPv4/IPv6, 16 IP interfaces. Management: web GUI over IPv4/IPv6 with HTTPS, CLI, Telnet, SSH/SFTP, SNMP v1/v2c/v3, sFlow, RMON, LLDP/LLDP-MED, dual images and dual configuration files, ZTP and DHCP auto-configuration. Green: EEE, per-port power saving, time-based PoE (PoE models). Hardware Rev A1, 19-inch 1U, 100-240 VAC, operating range -5 to 50 C, EMI Class A.",
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.dlink.com/us/en/-/media/business_products/dgs/dgs-1520/datasheet/dgs1520seriesa1datasheetv104ww.pdf"
